  "description": "PEYTOG crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P 1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C104 H86 Eu2 N4 O26 Ti4. From the CIF bond table, Eu1 (Eu) has 6 O neighbors; Eu2 (Eu) has 6 O neighbors; Ti1 (Ti) has 6 O neighbors; Ti4 (Ti) has 6 O neighbors; Ti2 (Ti) has 6 O neighbors; Ti3 (Ti) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 2.855-3.775 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 96.49-143.52°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula Eu2Ti4(μ2-O)2(μ3-O)4(−pbpy)2(ba)10. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ2-O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 μ3-O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
